# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
# 
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
# 
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD frame-1 64178 lightgray
ADD conn-1 39793 black
WHY Starts with two 5x11 frames joined by a connector beam, the base of the gearbox.
STEP 2
ADD frame-2 64178 lightgray
ADD conn-2 39793 black
WHY Adds the second long frame on the other side, mirroring step 1.
STEP 3
ADD pin-1 2780 black
ADD pin-2 2780 black
WHY Pins the two side frames into place.
STEP 4
ADD pin-3 2780 black
ADD pin-4 2780 black
WHY Pins the remaining corners, locking the base box together.
STEP 5
ADD topframe-1 39794 black
WHY Adds the 7x11 top frame over the base box.
STEP 6
ADD hub-1 18654 black
WHY Pins the top frame to the base with a round connector.
STEP 7
ADD hub-2 22961 black
WHY Starts a separate sub-assembly: a hub with one axle hole.
STEP 8
ADD pin-5 3673 lightgray
WHY Adds a smooth pin into the hub sub-assembly.
STEP 9
ADD hub-3 22961 black
ADD gear-1 6589 tan
ADD gear-1b 6589 tan
ADD gear-1c 6589 tan
WHY Adds a second hub and three bevel gears to the clutch sub-assembly.
STEP 10
ADD pin-6 32556 tan
ADD pin-7 32556 tan
WHY Adds two long pins through the clutch hub.
STEP 11
ADD hub-4 32039 lightgray
ADD pin-8 3673 lightgray
WHY Adds a connector and a smooth pin to the clutch sub-assembly.
STEP 12
ADD hub-5 22961 black
WHY Adds the last connector hub, finishing the clutch core.
STEP 13
ADD conn-3 32184 darkgray
ADD conn-4 6536 darkgray
WHY Starts a second sub-assembly: a perpendicular connector pair for the output shaft.
STEP 14
ADD pin-9 32002 tan
WHY Adds a 3/4 pin into the connector pair.
STEP 15
WHY No new parts - joins the clutch core (steps 7-12) to the connector pair (step 13).
STEP 16
WHY No new parts - extends the joined sub-assembly's connection into the frame.
STEP 17
WHY No new parts - drops the clutch/connector sub-assembly into the main frame.
STEP 18
ADD axle-1 32073 yellow
WHY Adds the first axle through the clutch assembly.
STEP 19
ADD axle-2 32073 yellow
WHY Adds a second axle, extending the shaft the other way.
STEP 20
ADD gear-2 18946 red
WHY Adds the first 16-tooth clutch gear onto the shaft.
STEP 21
ADD gear-3 18946 red
ADD gear-4 18946 red
WHY Adds the remaining two 16-tooth clutch gears, completing the one-way clutch stack.
STEP 22
ADD diffgear-1 6573 red
WHY Adds the 24-16 tooth differential-style gear with the built-in yellow driving ring.
STEP 23
WHY No new parts - drops the finished gear stack into the main frame.
STEP 24
ADD axle-3 32073 yellow
ADD axle-4 3706 black
WHY Adds the input and output axles through the gear stack.
STEP 25
ADD arm-1 42003 lightgray
WHY Starts a new lever sub-assembly: a perpendicular connector with two pin holes.
STEP 26
ADD ball-1 2736 lightgray
ADD ball-2 2736 lightgray
ADD pin-10 32556 tan
WHY Adds a towball and a long pin to the lever arm.
STEP 27
ADD arm-2 42003 lightgray
WHY Adds a second connector, mirroring step 25.
STEP 28
WHY No new parts - attaches the lever sub-assembly to the main frame.
STEP 29
ADD pin-11 6536 darkgray
ADD latch-1 32013 red
WHY Adds a pin and the angled connector that acts as the shift catch.
STEP 30
ADD pin-12 2780 black
ADD axle-5 87083 darkgray
WHY Adds a pin and a stopped axle locking the catch mechanism in place.
STEP 31
ADD conn-5 60483 orange
WHY Adds an orange connector marking the shift position.
STEP 32
ADD hub-6 22961 black
WHY Adds another hub to the shifting mechanism.
STEP 33
ADD pin-13 2780 black
ADD pin-14 2780 black
ADD pin-15 2780 black
ADD pin-16 2780 black
WHY Pins the whole gear cluster and shift mechanism firmly into the frame.
STEP 34
ADD gear-6 94925 lightgray
ADD conn-6 42003 lightgray
WHY Starts the output-shaft sub-assembly: a 16-tooth reinforced gear on a connector.
STEP 35
ADD axle-6 24316 reddishbrown
ADD gear-7 94925 lightgray
WHY Adds a stopped axle and a second reinforced gear.
STEP 36
ADD axle-7 4519 lightgray
ADD hub-7 32039 lightgray
WHY Extends the output shaft with another short axle and connector.
STEP 37
ADD axle-8 4519 lightgray
WHY Extends the shaft further.
STEP 38
ADD pin-17 18654 black
ADD bush-1 3713 red
WHY Joins the output shaft to a connector hub partway along its length.
STEP 39
WHY No new parts - caps the output shaft against the existing connector.
STEP 40
WHY No new parts - drops the finished output shaft sub-assembly into the main frame.
STEP 41
ADD gear-8 94925 lightgray
ADD gear-8b 94925 lightgray
ADD gear-8c 94925 lightgray
WHY Adds three more reinforced gears onto the output shaft.
STEP 42
ADD pin-18 18654 black
ADD pin-19 32039 lightgray
WHY Pins the output gear in place.
STEP 43
ADD axle-9 4519 lightgray
ADD axle-10 4519 lightgray
WHY Adds two more short axles, meshing the drive train.
STEP 44
ADD bush-2 32123b lightgray
WHY Adds a half bush, finishing the gear train support.
STEP 45
ADD pin-20 59443 yellow
ADD pulley-1 4185 lightgray
WHY Adds the output pulley (wedge belt wheel) on its own connector.
STEP 46
ADD pin-21 32184 darkgray
ADD gear-9 32270 black
WHY Adds the 12-tooth double bevel gear that drives the pulley shaft.
STEP 47
ADD pin-22 59443 yellow
ADD cap-1 35186 yellow
